{
 "format": "ainext.family/1",
 "id": "tpl:pp3u2-2-2:ratio-lin",
 "kind": "family",
 "lo_id": "lo:pp3u2-2-2",
 "parent_question_id": "none-provided",
 "source_page": null,
 "tier": "standard",
 "answer_type": "expression",
 "context": null,
 "params": [
  {
   "name": "n",
   "randint": [
    1,
    9
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "m",
   "randint": [
    2,
    9
   ],
   "resample_while": "m == n or gcd(m, n) != 1"
  },
  {
   "name": "p",
   "randint": [
    1,
    4
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "q",
   "randint": [
    1,
    4
   ]
  },
  {
   "require": "p * m > q * n",
   "why": "keep denominator positive"
  },
  {
   "name": "num",
   "let": "p * m + q * n"
  },
  {
   "name": "den",
   "let": "p * m - q * n"
  },
  {
   "name": "g",
   "let": "gcd(num, den)"
  },
  {
   "name": "n2",
   "let": "num // g"
  },
  {
   "name": "d2",
   "let": "den // g"
  },
  {
   "require": "d2 > 1",
   "why": "answer is a proper fraction not an integer"
  }
 ],
 "constraints": [
  "gcd(m, n) == 1"
 ],
 "stem": "If $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{{=m}}{{=n}}$, find the value of $\\frac{{=p}a+{=q}b}{{=p}a-{=q}b}$ as a fraction in its simplest form.",
 "answer": "",
 "solution": [
  "Since $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{{=m}}{{=n}}$, put $a={=m}k$ and $b={=n}k$ with $k\\neq 0$.",
  "Substitute: $\\frac{{=p}a+{=q}b}{{=p}a-{=q}b}=\\frac{{=p*m}k+{=q*n}k}{{=p*m}k-{=q*n}k}=\\frac{{=num}k}{{=den}k}$.",
  "Cancel $k$: $\\frac{{=num}}{{=den}}$, which in simplest form is $\\frac{{=n2}}{{=d2}}$."
 ],
